# Claude Code
# CLAUDE.md is shared and stays in the repo — it is the rules for this project,
# and the README points at it. Only per-machine state is ignored. There is no
# .claude/ directory at present; these lines are here so that if one is ever
# added, the local half of it cannot land in a commit.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tooling, if any is ever added. This repo has no build step by design; these
# are here so a stray install or script run cannot land in a commit.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Scratch: throwaway pages at the root, used while building (size checks,
# side-by-side comparisons). Scoped to root-level .html so it cannot swallow
# _template/, which is part of the repo.
/_*.html

# Scratch notes at the root, same idea and the same scoping. A handoff or a
# to-do list is written to be read once and thrown away, and one of them was
# committed and shipped for a fortnight before anyone noticed — it carried a
# local path, a build-environment note and a list of what had not been tested
# yet. README.md and CLAUDE.md are named explicitly so this cannot reach them;
# a study's own notes.md is never at the root, so it is untouched either way.
/_*.md
/HANDOFF*.md
/NOTES*.md
/TODO*.md
/SCRATCH*.md
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# One reference image is not ours to redistribute.
# 2026-09-raster-pulse/ref.png is a poster set carrying someone else's brand —
# the logo, the wordmark and the tagline — and a public repo redistributes it
# whole, which the study itself is careful not to do. The Inspiration line in
# that folder's notes.md still says where the build came from, which is the
# part a reader needs. Nothing links ref.png in any case: the index and every
# demo page show preview.html, the live component.
2026-09-raster-pulse/ref.png

# Skills are personal, not repo content. A skill installed to the account is
# available in every session and every repo — putting one here would scope it
# to this project and publish it with the code.
.claude/skills/
